;/a&gt;<![CDATA[In a heated exchange, Tamil Nadu chief minister C Joseph Vijay pointed fingers at the former DMK administration for alleged corruption linked to library book purchases. It has come to light that almost 1,800 artificially generated books were bought at excessive prices. Author Perumal Murugan raised concerns, leading Congress's Manickam Tagore to insist on a full inquiry.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/1800-fake-ai-books-inflated-prices-periyar-library-pits-cm-vijay-against-dmk/articleshow/135606488.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/1800-fake-ai-books-inflated-prices-periyar-library-pits-cm-vijay-against-dmk/articleshow/135606488.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-06T17:49:07+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Rajeev Singh</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135607313,imgsize-79090.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['Inviting death': Jharkhand tribal leader dies by suicide after emotional Facebook Live post]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/jharkhand-tribal-leader-dies-by-suicide-after-facebook-live-on-alleged-threats/articleshow/135605914.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135605914.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Nisha Kumari Bhagat, a prominent tribal leader in Jharkhand, was tragically found dead at her home in Ranchi. Just hours prior, she had gone live on Facebook, voicing concerns about threats from governmental bodies and land brokers. While police have indicated a possible suicide, they are actively probing the details surrounding her untimely death.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/jharkhand-tribal-leader-dies-by-suicide-after-facebook-live-on-alleged-threats/articleshow/135605914.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/jharkhand-tribal-leader-dies-by-suicide-after-facebook-live-on-alleged-threats/articleshow/135605914.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-06T17:06:45+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Rajeev Singh</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135606035,imgsize-98434.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[CBI books Future Retail Ltd, key promoters in Rs 904-crore bank fraud case]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/cbi-books-future-retail-ltd-key-promoters-in-rs-904-crore-bank-fraud-case/articleshow/135605098.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135605098.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[CBI has registered a major bank fraud concerning Future Retail Ltd. and its top executives for bank fraud. This case, involving  Rs 904 crore, follows a complaint from State Bank of India regarding fund misappropriation. Search operations were conducted at various locations linked to the firm's promoters, leading to the recovery of important documents. The company reportedly diverted bank funds through associated entities without using them for the intended purposes.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/cbi-books-future-retail-ltd-key-promoters-in-rs-904-crore-bank-fraud-case/articleshow/135605098.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/cbi-books-future-retail-ltd-key-promoters-in-rs-904-crore-bank-fraud-case/articleshow/135605098.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-06T16:59:31+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Raj Shekhar Jha</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135605798,imgsize-44628.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[You can own the world and still feel poor: Aruna Lohia Goenka on the magic of abundance]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/you-can-own-the-world-and-still-feel-poor-aruna-lohia-goenka-on-the-magic-of-abundance/articleshow/135605110.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135605110.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/you-can-own-the-world-and-still-feel-poor-aruna-lohia-goenka-on-the-magic-of-abundance/articleshow/135605110.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/you-can-own-the-world-and-still-feel-poor-aruna-lohia-goenka-on-the-magic-of-abundance/articleshow/135605110.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-06T16:41:41+05:30</pubDate><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135605227,imgsize-132640.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[EC gives voters excluded from draft electoral rolls in 7 states another chance to apply]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/ec-gives-voters-excluded-from-draft-electoral-rolls-in-7-states-another-chance-to-apply/articleshow/135604039.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135604039.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/ec-gives-voters-excluded-from-draft-electoral-rolls-in-7-states-another-chance-to-apply/articleshow/135604039.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/ec-gives-voters-excluded-from-draft-electoral-rolls-in-7-states-another-chance-to-apply/articleshow/135604039.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-06T16:16:12+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Karan Manral</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135604425,imgsize-102730.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Watch: Karmabhoomi Express coaches gutted in Punjab; short-circuit suspected]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/watch-karmabhoomi-express-coaches-gutted-in-punjab-short-circuit-suspected/articleshow/135602316.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135602316.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[A fire erupted in three coaches of the Karmabhoomi Express in Patiala district, Punjab on Friday around 1pm. The sudden flames instilled fear in passengers as they spread quickly. Promptly, railway officials and emergency teams arrived to manage the situation, which was likely caused by a short circuit. Fortunately, all passengers were unharmed, and alternative transportation was arranged for their continued journey.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/watch-karmabhoomi-express-coaches-gutted-in-punjab-short-circuit-suspected/articleshow/135602316.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/watch-karmabhoomi-express-coaches-gutted-in-punjab-short-circuit-suspected/articleshow/135602316.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-06T15:32:17+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Aastha Jha</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135602903,imgsize-14945861.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[SC ends decades-old power tussle, Himachal to get 11,973 MU from Punjab, Haryana]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/sc-ends-decades-old-power-tussle-himachal-to-get-11973-mu-from-punjab-haryana/articleshow/135600859.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135600859.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/sc-ends-decades-old-power-tussle-himachal-to-get-11973-mu-from-punjab-haryana/articleshow/135600859.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/sc-ends-decades-old-power-tussle-himachal-to-get-11973-mu-from-punjab-haryana/articleshow/135600859.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-06T15:16:52+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Vijaya Srivastava</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135602221,imgsize-104382.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[OBC creamy layer row: SC protects past jobs, promotions but leaves pending cases open]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/obc-creamy-layer-row-sc-protects-past-jobs-promotions-but-leaves-pending-cases-open/articleshow/135601416.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135601416.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[The Supreme Court has clarified that its March ruling will not impact completed appointments or promotions. Cases still pending will be examined individually by the courts based on merit and eligibility. The government expressed concerns that retrospective application could unsettle established positions and admissions. It sought two years to establish a uniform creamy layer mechanism across various sectors.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/obc-creamy-layer-row-sc-protects-past-jobs-promotions-but-leaves-pending-cases-open/articleshow/135601416.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/obc-creamy-layer-row-sc-protects-past-jobs-promotions-but-leaves-pending-cases-open/articleshow/135601416.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-06T14:53:01+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Rajeev Singh</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135601825,imgsize-134338.cms"/></item><item><title><![CD